From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AdvancedSettings: name half and full over-under 3D as top-bottom

The top-bottom name pattern knew only "tab" and "htab", so a film named
"Half-OU", "H-OU" or "HOU" - the usual names for over-under - played as
2D with its two halves stacked, while its side-by-side neighbour was
found. Take "ou" as well, alone or after "h", "half" or "full". It only
counts where the 3D pattern matched too, so ".Ou." in a title without a
3D token is not read as 3D.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/settings/AdvancedSettings.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/settings/AdvancedSettings.cpp
@@ -532,7 +532,7 @@
 
   m_stereoscopicregex_3d = "[-. _]3d[-. _]";
   m_stereoscopicregex_sbs = "[-. _]h?sbs[-. _]";
-  m_stereoscopicregex_tab = "[-. _]h?tab[-. _]";
+  m_stereoscopicregex_tab = "[-. _](h|half|full)?[-. _]?(tab|ou)[-. _]";
   m_stereoscopicregex_mvc = "[-. _]h?mvc[-. _]";
 
   m_logLevelHint = m_logLevel = LOG_LEVEL_NORMAL;
